---
import Legal from '@/layouts/Legal.astro';
import { APP_URL } from '@/lib';
---

<Legal
  title="Data deletion"
  description="How to delete your LeadWave data, and how someone who messaged a Page can have their data removed. Required by Meta's platform terms."
  updated="18 September 2026"
>
  <p>
    Meta requires every app on its platform to publish a clear route to deleting
    data. This is ours. There are three situations, and they have different
    answers.
  </p>

  <h2>You want to delete your LeadWave account</h2>
  <ol class="mb-5 list-decimal pl-5 [&_li]:mb-1.5 [&_li]:text-[14.5px] [&_li]:leading-relaxed [&_li]:text-body">
    <li>
      Open <a href={`${APP_URL}/settings`}>Settings</a> in the dashboard.
    </li>
    <li>Disconnect each connected Page. Its access token is deleted immediately.</li>
    <li>Delete the workspace.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Everything belonging to that workspace — contacts, conversations, messages,
    leads, automations, AI knowledge, bio pages and analytics — is removed within
    30 days. Backups are rotated on the same schedule, so a copy does not survive
    in cold storage beyond that.
  </p>

  <h2>You want to disconnect one Page but keep the account</h2>
  <p>
    Disconnect it in Settings. The Page's access token is deleted immediately and
    the data attached to that Page is removed within 30 days. Nothing belonging to
    your other Pages is affected — in LeadWave, contacts, automations and AI
    knowledge are scoped per Page and never shared between two.
  </p>

  <h2>You messaged a Page that uses LeadWave</h2>
  <p>
    If you sent a message to a business's Facebook Page and want the record of it
    removed, the business controls that data, not us. There are two routes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Ask the business directly.</strong> They can delete your contact
      record, which removes your conversation, your messages and anything captured
      from you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Remove the app's access on Facebook.</strong> In your Facebook
      settings, under Apps and Websites, removing the app sends us a deletion
      signal which we honour.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can also ask a business to stop messaging you at all. LeadWave records
    that as an opt-out on your contact, which excludes you from every automation,
    every AI reply and every export from that point on.
  </p>

  <h2>Deletion callback</h2>
  <p>
    LeadWave implements Meta's data deletion callback. When Facebook tells us a
    person has removed the app, we delete the records associated with that
    person's Page-scoped id and confirm it back to Facebook with a tracking
    reference, as the platform terms require.
  </p>

  <h2>What we keep, and why</h2>
  <p>
    After a deletion we retain only what we are legally required to: billing
    records for tax purposes, and a minimal audit entry recording that a deletion
    happened and when. Neither contains message content, contact details or
    captured leads.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Trouble with any of the above — email
    <a href="mailto:leadwaveonline@gmail.com">leadwaveonline@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
